# Agent Toolstack — Shared Knowledge (OpenCode + MiMoCode)

Curated facts about this machine's AI coding setup. Read this before designing UI,
wiring MCP servers, or touching config. Verified = checked against the live system
(2026-10-17). Unverified = reported by a source, not confirmed here.

## Environment

- macOS (darwin), user `likeanew`, Apple Silicon.
- Primary project: `/Users/likeanew/Documents/CollegeStat`
  - `collegestat/` — the main app (48 entries, modified Oct 15).
  - `AI-Setup/` — scratch workspace (empty as of 2026-10-17).
- Two coding agents installed side by side: **OpenCode** (`~/.config/opencode`) and
  **MiMoCode** (`~/.config/mimocode`, binary `~/.mimocode/bin/mimo`, v0.1.15).
- Other agent configs present: `~/.codex` (Codex, 3.6 GB — large), `~/.cursor`,
  `~/.gemini`, `~/.copilot`, `~/.agents`.

## MCP config format (identical in OpenCode and MiMoCode)

```jsonc
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",          // or https://mimo.xiaomi.com/mimocode/config.json
  "mcp": {
    "name":  { "type": "local",  "command": ["npx", "-y", "pkg"] },
    "docs":  { "type": "remote", "url": "https://host/mcp" },
    "off":   { "enabled": false }                          // disable without deleting
  }
}
```

**Do NOT use `"mcp_servers"` or a `command` string + `args` array.** That format is
wrong for both tools. The correct key is `"mcp"` and `command` is an array.

## Verified MCP toolstack (installed in both agents)

| Server | What it gives you | When to use |
|---|---|---|
| `inspo` | 2,320 real-site captures: palettes, fonts, macrostructures, 68 reference components with copy-pasteable JSX. stdio via `inspo-mcp`; hosted `https://inspomcp.dev/api/mcp` also works. | Any UI/design task — call `recommend(brief)` first |
| `shadcn` | Browse/view/install real shadcn/ui + any registry component. `npx shadcn@latest mcp`. | Component work — prevents hallucinated component code |
| `context7` | Up-to-date library docs + code examples. Remote `https://mcp.context7.com/mcp`. | When unsure of an API/version |
| `animotion` | 745 hand-crafted CSS3 animations + 9,740 real SVG icons (Lucide/Tabler/Heroicons/Bootstrap). `npx animotion-mcp`. | Animation + icons — kills AI-looking generated icons |
| `gsap-master` | GSAP expert: intent→60fps code, plugins (SplitText, ScrollTrigger, DrawSVG), debugging, perf optimizer. `npx @vinhnguyen/gsap-mcp`. | Complex animation, scroll systems, text reveals |
| `playwright` | Browser automation, screenshots, accessibility snapshots, speed/QA checks. Runs `--headless --isolated`. | Visual verification, E2E, performance |
| `sequential-thinking` | Structured step-by-step reasoning. | Complex architecture / debugging |
| `lemma` | Persistent local memory over MCP (confidence decay, guides, JSONL/SQLite). `npx lemma-mcp`. | Cross-session recall; `memory_read` first, `memory_add` after |
| `supabase` / `prisma` / `github` | DB + GitHub. Remote, **require OAuth login** (`mimo mcp auth <name>`). | Backend / repo work once authenticated |

### MCP gotchas (verified from the live log)

- The 3 auth-required servers spam ~600 WARN lines per session until logged in.
  Run `mimo mcp auth supabase` (and `prisma`, `github`) or set `"enabled": false`.
- `shadcn` logs `MCP error -32601: Method not found` for `resources` — harmless;
  the server exposes tools only, not the resources method OpenCode/MiMo probe.
- Local servers spawn via `npx`; first run downloads the package (a few seconds).

## Config & skill locations

**OpenCode**
- Global config: `~/.config/opencode/opencode.jsonc`
- Skills: `~/.agents/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`, `~/.config/opencode/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`,
  `.opencode/skills/`, `.claude/skills/` (project), plus `~/.claude/skills/`
- Verify: `opencode mcp list`, `opencode debug config`, `opencode reload`

**MiMoCode**
- Global config: `~/.config/mimocode/mimocode.jsonc` (JSONC, merges over defaults)
- Project config: `<project>/.mimocode/mimocode.jsonc`
- Skills: `~/.agents/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` (global), `<project>/.mimocode/skills/`,
  `.agents/skills/`, `.claude/skills/`, `.codex/skills/` (brand roots opt-in via env)
- Agents/modes: `~/.config/mimocode/agent/<name>.md` or `<project>/.mimocode/agent/<name>.md`
- Commands: `.mimocode/command/<name>.md`
- Memory: `~/.local/share/mimocode/memory/projects/<project>/MEMORY.md`, `.../global/MEMORY.md`
- Verify: `mimo mcp list`, `mimo debug config`, `mimo debug skill`, `mimo agent list`
- Default model: `mimo/mimo-auto` (free, 1M context). Models: `mimo models`.

**Shared skill path:** `~/.agents/skills/` is read by BOTH agents — put cross-tool
knowledge here (this skill lives there).

## Known issues on this machine (2026-10-17)

- **GitLab auth expired** — `GitLabError: 401 Unauthorized` for `gitlab/duo-chat-fable-5`.
  Re-authenticate GitLab; token last refreshed 2026-10-06.
- **`.codex` is 3.6 GB** — `sessions/` alone is 2.3 GB (369 rollout `.jsonl.zst`
  files), `thread_history_1.sqlite` 592 MB. Clean old sessions if disk is tight.
- **Stale lock files** in `~/.codex` (0-byte `.sqlite-maintenance.lock`, empty
  `*.sqlite-wal`, empty `AGENTS.md`, `transcription-history.jsonl`). Safe to remove.
- **`.codex-global-state.json.bak`** is a byte-identical duplicate of the live state file.
- **No DB corruption**: `opencode.db` (140 MB) and all Codex sqlite files pass
  `PRAGMA integrity_check` / `quick_check`.
- **OpenCode log** is 16 MB at `~/.local/share/opencode/log/opencode.log`; rotate if large.

## Tools reported by awesome-opencode but NOT installable as-is

`morph-fast-apply`, `crawlberg`, `harness-memory`, `flowdeck`, `honcho`,
`opencode-mission-control` are GitHub-only repos, not npm packages — they need manual
clone + plugin-file placement. `@seos/*` (AISEOS) is GitHub-only and unverified.
`@inspo/mcp-server` does not exist on npm — the correct package is `inspo-mcp`.

## Working conventions

- Prefer real, verified tools over generated approximations: `inspo` for design,
  `animotion` for icons/animations, `shadcn` for components, `context7` for APIs.
- Keep config edits minimal and targeted; preserve JSONC comments and `$schema`.
- After editing config, reload (`opencode reload`) or restart (`mimo`) before verifying.
- Treat API keys as secrets: never echo them into logs, diffs, or responses.

